<title>USA: U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</title>
<headline>U.S. interest rates higher in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve announced average interest rates for the week ended Sept 6, compared with the Aug 30 week, as follows:</p>
<p>   Federal funds rate.................5.39 vs 5.21</p>
<p>   3-month Treasury bills.............5.19 vs 5.09</p>
<p>   3-month commercial paper...........5.55 vs 5.43</p>
<p>   3-month bankers acceptances........5.44 vs 5.33</p>
<p>   3-month CDs........................5.55 vs 5.42</p>
<p>   3-month Eurodollar.................5.51 vs 5.40</p>
<p>   30-year Government bond............7.11 vs 7.03</p>
</text>
